To determine the morphology of MOF particles, SEM was performed. The results revealed that the powder consists of quasi-spherical particles with the sizes of \( 100{-}300\ \mathrm{nm} \) (Figure S6), which were not suitable for single-crystal analysis. Therefore, their structures were determined from synchrotron PXRD. XRD indexing and Rietveld analysis was performed

with TOPAS version 5. Figure 2 shows the XRD profiles of VPI-100 (Cu) and VPI-100 (Ni) at room temperature. Both patterns have intense low angle peaks, which are commonly seen in XRD of porous structures. The high similarity between the as-synthesized VPI-100 (Cu) and VPI-100 (Ni) patterns suggests they are isostructural. Crystallographic data for VPI-100 is summarized in Table 1. Further details about structure determination and refinement are summarized in the Supporting Information (Section 3).

VPI-100 (Cu) and VPI-100 (Ni) crystallize in the space group \( I\!4/m \). In the structural models, each MOF node is comprised of a \( \mathrm{Zr}_{6}(\mu_{3}{\mathrm{-OH}})_{8}(\mathrm{OH})_{8}(\mu^{2}\eta^{2}{\mathrm{-}}(\mathrm{O}_{2}\mathrm{C})_{2}\mathrm{cyclam})_{8} \) cluster \( \mathrm{Zr}_{6} \)-cluster) that is centered at \( I \)-lattice positions (i.e. unit cell origin and body center) with site symmetry \( 4/m \) \( (\mathrm{D}_{4h}) \). Similar to 8-connected \( \mathrm{Zr}_{6} \) cluster in PCN-222 and \( \mathrm{NU}{-}1000^{39} \), the \( \mathrm{Zr} \)-atoms of the \( \mathrm{Zr}_{6} \)-cluster occupy the corners of a distorted octahedron; each 8-coordinate \( \mathrm{Zr}^{4+} \) has a distorted square antiprism geometry (Figure. 3A). The faces of the octahedron defined by the \( 6\,Z\mathbf{r} \)-atoms are capped by \( \mu_{3}{\mathrm{-OH}} \) groups that fill 4 coordination sites around each \( \mathrm{Zr}^{4+} \). Eight cyclam ligands are coordinated to each cluster with each carboxylate bridging between an axial \( \mathrm{Zr}^{4+} \) and equatorial \( \mathrm{Zr}^{4+} \) of \( \mathrm{Zr}_{6} \)-octahedron. The coordination sphere around each equatorial \( \mathrm{Zr} \)-atom is completed by two terminal -OH groups.

Each \( \mathrm{Zr}_{6} \)-cluster is linked to the eight nearest clusters via the eight cyclam ligands that lie parallel to the unit cell body diagonals (Figure. 3B). The resulting 3D frameworks exhibit \( \mathrm{CsCl} \) topology (Schläfli symbol of \( 4^{3-}\mathrm{O} \)). Disordered solvents and chloride ions occupy the pores. Because the PXRD data resolution is relatively low \( (\sim\!1.8\,\mathrm{~\AA~}) \), the solvents and/ions content within the pores could not be definitively identified (see Supporting Information, Section 3). After removing the solvent/ion contents from pores, void calculation in Mercury give a contact surface void volume of \( 2663.51\mathrm{~\AA~}^{3} \) (48.3% of cell) and a solvent accessible void volume of \( 1306.03\,\mathrm{~\AA~}^{3} \) (23.7% of cell) for VPI-100 (Cu). Corresponding volumes for VPI-100 (Ni) are \( 2569.44\,\mathrm{~\AA~}^{3} \) (47.6%) and \( 1237.52\,\mathrm{~\AA~}^{3} \) (22.9%).

